 :root-cause
 "Generated-authoritative can? always initialized the forward indexed traversal from the subject. A point query is anchored by one resource, but forward evaluation can enumerate every resource reachable from a broad subject before finding that target. Making generated authority the release default therefore changed a target-local authorization check into work proportional to subject fanout."
 :fix
 "Initialize the already-verified reverse indexed traversal from the concrete resource and use its Boolean renderer to stop when the requested subject is emitted or to exhaust the target-local reverse search before returning false. Add a direction regression and a 16-versus-1,040 reachable-resource logical/backend-work gate."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.formal.state-trace-differential-test/generated-mode-routes-and-does-not-reorder-acyclic-multipath-pages"
